The correct nested structure is `vite.environments.client.build.rollupOptions.output`:

```js
export default defineConfig({
  vite: {
    environments: {
      client: {
        build: {
          rollupOptions: {
            output: {
              entryFileNames: 'js/[name]-[hash].js',
              chunkFileNames: 'js/chunks/[name]-[hash].js',
              assetFileNames: 'static/[name]-[hash][extname]',
            },
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

This scoping to the client environment was introduced in Astro 6.0; in Astro 5.x these options were configured at `vite.build.rollupOptions.output`.

Set `vite.environments.client.build.rollupOptions.output.entryFileNames` in `astro.config.mjs`:

```js
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
export default defineConfig({
  vite: {
    environments: {
      client: {
        build: {
          rollupOptions: {
            output: {
              entryFileNames: 'js/[name]-[hash].js',
            },
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

