Create a custom logger module that exports a default function returning an `AstroLoggerDestination` with a `write()` method. The `write()` method receives an `AstroLoggerMessage` object containing `message`, `label`, `level`, and `time` properties. Use `matchesLevel()` from `astro/logger` to filter by log level. Write the structured message to a file using Node's `fs` module.

```js
// @org/custom-logger/index.js
import { matchesLevel } from "astro/logger";
import { appendFileSync } from "fs";

function fileLogger({ level = "info", filePath = "./app.log" } = {}) {
  return {
    write(message) {
      if (matchesLevel(message.level, level)) {
        const logEntry = JSON.stringify(message) + "\n";
        appendFileSync(filePath, logEntry);
      }
    },
  };
}
export default fileLogger;
```

