Extend the `Astro.CustomImageProps` interface (added in `astro@5.16.6`) with your service's extra props, then expose those types through an integration using the `injectTypes()` helper:

```ts
declare namespace Astro {
  interface CustomImageProps {
    /** Apply a Gaussian blur with this radius to the image. */
    blur?: number;
  }
}
```

Once exposed via `injectTypes()`, users get autocomplete and type checking on `<Image>`, `<Picture>`, and `getImage()` — e.g. passing `blur="yes"` errors with "Type 'string' is not assignable to type 'number | undefined'."

The `config` property is a serializable object used for identification. It stores the provider configuration (e.g., API tokens, endpoints) passed when the provider is instantiated in `astro.config.ts`, making it available to `init()` and `resolveFont()`.
```ts
export function registryFontProvider(config: { token: string }): FontProvider {
  return { name: "registry", config, init: async () => { data = await retrieveFonts(config.token); }, ... };
}
```
